id: hac-fj2b
title: Add agent-native frontend semantic catalog discovery
description: "Expose current official Home Assistant frontend version, theme, icon, and translation WebSocket contracts through typed, bounded, format-safe hassio commands while retaining raw ws call passthrough."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,api,frontend,home-assistant,localization,websocket
created_at: "2026-08-07T05:47:24.265Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T06:35:28.115Z"
deadline: "2026-08-08T05:47:24.265Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "Typed commands cover frontend/get_version, frontend/get_themes, frontend/get_icons, and frontend/get_translations with input validation and bounded output; every command has detailed help and all six output formats remain valid; exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage and strict repository gates pass; read-only live acceptance passes against the configured Home Assistant instance without persisting private payloads"
definition_of_ready: All-status duplicate search is clean for this scope; current official Core schemas and live instance support are confirmed; prior WebSocket lineages and repository conventions are understood.
goal: best-agent-home-assistant-cli
objective: typed-frontend-semantic-catalog
value: Agents can discover version-specific visual semantics and localized labels without hand-authoring raw protocol payloads.
impact: "Improves deterministic planning, accessible presentation, localization, and forward-compatible automation generation."
outcome: A documented typed frontend discovery family with bounded machine-readable results and live proof.
why_now: Home Assistant removed translated action descriptions from get_services and current Core exposes dedicated icon and translation catalogs; the CLI lacks a discoverable typed surface.
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: medium
confidence: 97
sprint: frontend-intelligence
release: 2026.8.7
